{
  "_doc": "MOBILE INFANTRY — Federal Service, Terran Federation. The total-conversion test: this pack shares NO platform, rank, billet or echelon with 1CD, and needed no engine change to author beyond the one it discovered (a formation whose elements hang directly off it, with no company rung). Organisation follows the novel — DIVISION -> REGIMENT -> COMPANY -> PLATOON, no brigade and no battalion — and the tone follows the film. The chair is a COMPANY: a Mobile Infantry captain runs a drop the way a battalion commander runs a fight.",

  "id": "mi",
  "name": "Mobile Infantry",
  "abbr": "MI",
  "nick": "First Division",
  "motto": "Everybody Fights, Nobody Quits",

  "_catalogs_doc": "Powered armour is not a truck with legs: a Marauder suit is WORN, so it is a troop kind and not a vehicle, and an MI platoon fields no vehicles at all. That is why every unit here is `mob: foot` and yet moves faster than a Stryker — the suit's jump jets are the mobility.",
