  "_formation_doc": "DIVISION -> REGIMENT -> COMPANY -> PLATOON, straight out of the novel: Rasczak's Roughnecks are formally 'Second Platoon, George Company, Third Regiment, First Division'. No brigade, no battalion. Companies are lettered and spoken phonetically (George, King), and written with their regiment because the letters repeat — G/3 is George Company of the Third, and it is the only G/3 in the division. chairRung 1 puts the player in a COMPANY commander's chair; the thing they field is a platoon, exactly as a US battalion commander fields a platoon one rung up.",
  "formation": {
    "chair": "G/3",
    "playable": "all",
    "top": { "name": "DIVISION", "mark": "XX" },
    "echelons": [
      { "name": "REGIMENT", "mark": "III" },
      { "name": "COMPANY", "mark": "I" }
    ],
    "chairRung": 1,
    "under": [
      {
        "desig": "DIV HQ", "nick": "First Division", "kind": "MI-DIV-HQ",
